{
  "$comment": "Registry of the addon repos under addons/. Managed by scripts/update-addon-repos.sh: 'devbox run update-addon-repos' (both), 'devbox run update-subtrees' or 'devbox run update-submodules'. Add an entry to vendor or link a repo; the same command adds it on the first run and updates it after that. Each entry needs a 'prefix' (e.g. addons/<repo>), a git 'url' and a 'branch' (your Odoo series, e.g. {{ odoo_version }}). Use 'subtrees' to vendor the files into this repo's own history (git subtree add/pull --squash, commits automatically), or 'submodules' to record a pointer to the other repo (git submodule add / update --remote, left staged for you to commit). A prefix belongs in one list only. Example: { \"prefix\": \"addons/queue\", \"url\": \"git@github.com:OCA/queue.git\", \"branch\": \"{{ odoo_version }}\" }",
